# Deploy / restart discipline (GOLDEN)

FIXED ops rule. Robb 2026-10-03 (updated same night): surprise restarts bad; Done-waits worse.
Robb later: **after a patch, always restart the servers that need the jar** unless he says otherwise.

## After a patch — restart (default)

- Deploy the jar(s), then **restart the server(s) that load them** (usually MMO-R; Hub/MMO-D only if that jar lives there too).
- Exception: Robb says **kein Restart** / **-NoRestart** / jars only → upload only.
- **Do not** restart unrelated servers “just in case”.

## When restarting — clean + finish immediately

Canonical: `C:\Users\Robbi\IdeaProjects\aetherion-ops\bin\ae.ps1`

```text
.\ae.ps1 restart <mmor|hub|…>
```

Graceful `stop` (LOCKED countdown) → clear `session.lock` → start → confirm java pid → **exit**.

- **Do NOT** pass `-Wait` unless he wants “wait until Done”.
- **Do NOT** poll `latest.log`, AwaitShell for `Done (`, or hang on a huge `block_until_ms`.
- When `ae.ps1 restart` returns: **done**. One short confirmation. No multi-minute hang.
- Prefer `stop` (not SIGKILL) so ShutdownCountdown runs.

## Agent shell hygiene

- Restart block ~60–90s max (stop+start pid). Then reply.
- Never chain “restart A → wait Done → restart B → wait Done” unless he ordered that sequence.
